@subsection Compilation Optimization Strategies

The compiler implements several optimization techniques applicable across languages:

@itemize
@item Type inference: Determining variable types at compile-time enables direct method calls instead of dynamic dispatch
@item Constant folding: Pre-computing arithmetic expressions with constant operands at compile-time
@item Inlining: Replacing method calls with the method body to eliminate call overhead
@item Loop optimization: Analyzing loops for invariant code motion and strength reduction
@item Specialization: Generating specialized code for common types (SmallInteger, Symbol, etc.)
@item Memoization: Caching expensive computations with constant parameters
@end itemize

